{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "list_id": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "run": 4,
  "simulation_id": "sim-02",
  "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round1_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B027",
        "laureates": [
          "Francis Halzen"
        ],
        "citation": "for opening high-energy neutrino astronomy as a new window on the universe"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B045",
    "B025"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "B027 remains my preferred achievement because it is a discovery in the most direct sense: nature has become observable through a previously inaccessible high-energy messenger. The result has endured for more than a decade and grown into a distinct observational field with multimessenger consequences. That combination of a new empirical clue about the violent universe, reproducibility of the programme, and lasting scientific reach is unusually compelling.",
    "case_against": "The serious weakness is attribution. IceCube is intrinsically a large collaboration, and selecting Halzen alone risks converting broad collective accomplishment into a personal discovery. We must establish that his scientific and institutional leadership was sufficiently decisive to meet the individual-credit standard, rather than merely prominent.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "pearce-mark",
        "point": "Pearce likewise regards B027 as a lasting breakthrough that opened a new observational window, while emphasizing that its credit compresses a large detector collaboration into one person.",
        "response": "I agree with both aspects. The collaboration issue is not a cosmetic qualification but the central question for B027; nevertheless, a collaboration-scale experiment should not be disqualified if one can document a genuinely indispensable scientific architect. The new observational capability and its mature astrophysical yield remain stronger than the attribution concern, subject to that documentation."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll argues that B045 has a particularly clean two-person attribution in Katori and Ye, coupled to mature, widely reproduced precision metrology.",
        "response": "This is a powerful alternative and its attribution is indeed much cleaner. I would still place B027 ahead because the neutrino result opens a qualitatively new route to observing the cosmos, whereas lattice clocks, however extraordinary, require us to distinguish a fundamental discovery from an exceptional and continuing refinement of measurement technology."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig stresses that B025 provides a theoretically clean, extensively tested account of nonequilibrium fluctuations with broad experimental reach.",
        "response": "B025 is an intellectually deep and mature alternative. My qualification is that its prize boundary and the hierarchy among related fluctuation relations require finer historical work, while B027 has a more discrete observational breakthrough with a particularly vivid connection between fundamental physics and nature."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether the evidentiary record can establish Halzen's individual contribution as sufficiently singular within the IceCube collaboration.",
      "Whether the discovery's most important astrophysical source identifications and interpretations are mature enough to define the citation narrowly."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
